The company's consistent growth has been attributed to its dominant position in government contracts and the expanding applications of Satori AI. However, analysts at the ''Okami Financial Chronicle'' have noted that profit margins have declined from 18.2% in 2020 to 15.8% in 2024, citing increased competition from [[Zong]] semiconductor manufacturers and rising research and development costs.

=== Controversies ===

==== Family dispute ====
In September 2025, Kizan's younger brother, [[Kizan Masahiro]], filed a lawsuit alleging that Toshiaki had improperly excluded him from the family trust. Masahiro, who owns 8% of Kizan Systems shares, claimed that his brother had pressured their elderly mother into changing her will to leave all family assets to Toshiaki. The case is pending in [[Okami District Court]], and legal analysts estimate it could take three to five years to resolve.

==== Data-Gate involvement ====
During the 2016 [[Data-Gate]] scandal, evidence emerged that early versions of Satori AI had been used to monitor domestic communications without proper warrants. Kizan Systems denied involvement, stating that the system had been "misused by third parties." An independent investigation by the [[Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications (Okaiken)|Ministry of Internal Affairs]] found no evidence of wrongdoing by the company, but recommended enhanced oversight of AI systems processing personal data.

==== Supply chain concerns ====
In 2024, a [[Fair Trade Commission (Okaiken)|Fair Trade Commission]] investigation revealed that Kizan Systems had pressured smaller suppliers into accepting below-market prices under threat of contract termination. The company agreed to a ¥12 billion settlement without admitting wrongdoing.

